                     <title>Horae S. Trinitatis</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">MLGB2 reports books at Syon Abbey (South
                        Brent); since 2004 these have been deposited in Exeter University
                        Library.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate>s. xv med</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#cl"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_537">Syon, Middlesex.
                        Bridgettine abbey of St Saviour, St Mary the Virgin, and St Bridget.
                        </orgName><p>At the end of the litany (and preceding the Office of the Dead)
                        is 'Anima regis henrici fundatoris nostri et anime omnium fidelium
                        defunctorum per misericordiam d. n. i. c. in pace requiescat Amen' (fol.
                        168v; cf. Cambridge, Magdalene College, MS 11, fol. 218v).</p><p>Obits for
                        Alice Langton (she is in the Martiloge of Syon); profession of William
                        Catesby 1488 (also in the Martiloge; a donor of books).</p><p>Two leaves,
                        which might have held inscriptions, are missing at the
                        beginning.</p><p> </p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Holleyman and Trencher (Brighton), cat. no. 7
                     (1949), item 224, purchased from 'a local man named A. W. Turner' (letter, 16
                     Novermber 1962).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Sold by them to the Abbess.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Since 2004 the Syon Abbey books have been
                     deposited in Exeter University Library.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"> </provenance>
               </history>
